question.:question/worked-solution:
First, compute the ordered cross product $\mathbf{b}\times\mathbf{c}$:

$$
\begin{aligned}
\mathbf{b}\times\mathbf{c}&=\begin{vmatrix}\mathbf{i}&\mathbf{j}&\mathbf{k}\\-2&-1&3\\1&1&1\end{vmatrix}
\end{aligned}
$$

Its components are

$$
\begin{aligned}
d_1&=(-1)\cdot1-3\cdot1=-4 \\
d_2&=-((-2)\cdot1-3\cdot1)=5 \\
d_3&=(-2)\cdot1-(-1)\cdot1=-1
\end{aligned}
$$

Thus $\mathbf{b}\times\mathbf{c}=\langle-4,5,-1\rangle$. Now take the dot product with $\mathbf{a}$:

$$
\begin{aligned}
\mathbf{a}\cdot(\mathbf{b}\times\mathbf{c})&=\langle-2,0,0\rangle\cdot\langle-4,5,-1\rangle \\
&=(-2)\cdot(-4)+0\cdot5+0\cdot(-1) \\
&=8+0+0 \\
&=8
\end{aligned}
$$

