question.:question/worked-solution:
Factor out the supplied scalar multipliers:

$$
\begin{aligned}
(\sqrt{2}\mathbf{a})\cdot\bigl(\mathbf{b}\times (3\mathbf{c})\bigr)&=2 \sqrt{2} \\
3 \sqrt{2}\bigl[\mathbf{a}\cdot\bigl(\mathbf{b}\times \mathbf{c}\bigr)\bigr]&=2 \sqrt{2} \\
\mathbf{a}\cdot\bigl(\mathbf{b}\times \mathbf{c}\bigr)&=\frac{2}{3}
\end{aligned}
$$

Swap $\mathbf{a}$ and $\mathbf{c}$; one swap reverses the sign:

$$
\begin{aligned}
\mathbf{c}\cdot\bigl(\mathbf{b}\times \mathbf{a}\bigr)&=- \frac{2}{3}
\end{aligned}
$$

The requested scalar is $- \frac{2}{3}$.

Factor out the supplied scalar multipliers:

$$
\begin{aligned}
(3\mathbf{b})\cdot\bigl((-3\mathbf{c})\times (-3\mathbf{a})\bigr)&=- \frac{81}{2} \\
27\bigl[\mathbf{b}\cdot\bigl(\mathbf{c}\times \mathbf{a}\bigr)\bigr]&=- \frac{81}{2} \\
\mathbf{b}\cdot\bigl(\mathbf{c}\times \mathbf{a}\bigr)&=- \frac{3}{2}
\end{aligned}
$$

Swap $\mathbf{c}$ and $\mathbf{a}$; one swap reverses the sign:

$$
\begin{aligned}
\mathbf{b}\cdot\bigl(\mathbf{a}\times \mathbf{c}\bigr)&=\frac{3}{2}
\end{aligned}
$$

The requested scalar is $\frac{3}{2}$.
